00,"description":"Wait for END and show tail"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_015WWjuMG2HeY5mDXchCs2dB","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && cat >> docs/violation-decisions.md <<'EOF'\n\n## repeated-failure-class — 2026-09-24 05:54 (cycle 71 judgement, after archive/peer/2026-09-24-retrospective-cycle71.md)\n\n`VIOLATION: repeated-failure-class | loss_min=57 | loss_usd=? | evidence=tools/hooks/material_marker.log:1265`.\nThe judgement session resumed a material agent with `SendMessage`, which runs it in the BACKGROUND, and then polled\nbuild logs for 57 minutes after that agent had already stopped on a gate refusal. This is the fourth consecutive\ncycle in which a judgement session mishandled background work.\n\nDECISION: device\n\nDevice: `tools/hooks/guard_session.py` refuses `SendMessage` to a `material` or `log-reader` agent inside a cycle\nsession (`CYCLE_SESSION=1`), with the message \"dispatch a NEW foreground Agent\". Every re-dispatch then blocks until\nit returns. Self-test: the refusal fires under `CYCLE_SESSION=1`, and the interactive chat is untouched. Scheduled\nafter L7-1b run 3 (deliverable first).\n\n## device-failed — 2026-09-24 05:54 (cycle 71 judgement, after archive/peer/2026-09-24-retrospective-cycle71.md)\n\n`VIOLATION: device-failed | loss_min=5 | loss_usd=? | evidence=stop_record@tools/hooks/material_marker.log:1264`.\n\nDECISION: device (repair of `tools/stop_record.py`)\n\n- The prior-art dispatch half is REPAIRED (05:31, bgrun `--` parsing, `selftest_stoprecord_bgrun.py` 6/0). This also\n  CLOSES the `--recipe=` gap named in the 03:53 block above.\n- Still to repair: the stop record also refuses READ-ONLY commands on a stopped recipe (`wc -l`, `sed -n`, an AST\n  parse; `material_marker.log:1256,1263,1274`). Refuse only commands that EXECUTE the recipe, and self-test both\n  directions.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Append the two dated decisions from the cycle-71 retrospective"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":7,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":7,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":7,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":4,"log-reader":3}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":61,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 71 is closed. The L7-1a intermediate is saved and accepted, but L7-1b ran twice this cycle and saved nothing, so L7-1b is still not delivered.\n\n**Delivered**\n- **L7-1a:** `claudeDev\\D1_l7_1a_20260924_035656.vi`, md5 `34aaadf1…`. `#376` is moved into loop 1.7 and the two new shift-register pairs exist, with nothing wired. It is broken by design and has never been run.\n- **Its one failed gate was our prediction, not the file.** Three extra edges disappeared from the graph after the move. A read-only diagnostic (9/0) showed the wires and their sinks are intact; the tunnels just lost their direction when `#376` left. The contract is now stricter (Pre-decided 172).\n- **Jev check, measured without LabVIEW:**\n  - The init row that failed last cycle went from p 0.584 to 0.906 once its question named the right terminal.\n  - A deliberately wrong pairing scored 0.098, so the Jev check does catch wrong sources (Pre-decided 171).\n- **Device repairs, each self-tested:**\n  - `guard_peer`: last cycle's early retry slipped through because the hook ran past its 15 s timeout. It now has a 10 s budget and blocks when that runs out.\n  - `bgrun`: Jev scripts no longer trip the failure scan.\n  - `stop_record`: it no longer blocks the prior-art review of a recipe.\n\n**Not delivered: L7-1b (wiring the 9 rows)**\n- Run 1 wired all 9 rows and passed its row checks. It then crashed in our verification step, which looked a terminal up by a name that changes once the wire lands.\n- Run 2 crashed earlier: the uid lookup built for run 1 was applied before the wires existed.\n- Both are bugs in our scripts with measured causes. The bed and L7-1a files are unchanged. The fix is recorded as Pre-decided 174.\n\n**My loss this cycle:** I resumed a finished material session in the background, then polled for about 57 minutes for a build that was never going to start. That time would have covered run 3 inside this cycle. The retrospective named it the top fault. The fix is a hook that refuses such resumes in cycle sessions, so every re-dispatch blocks until it returns.\n\n**NEXT (cycle 72), in one material dispatch:**\n1. Apply the Pre-decided 174 fix in `stagekit`.\n2. Get a prior-art review of the changed recipe.\n3. Push the recipe's real rows through the addressing code without LabVIEW.\n4. Run L7-1b a third time from the accepted L7-1a file.\n\nAfter that, build the two decided devices: the resume-refusing hook, and letting read-only commands past the stop record.\n\nRig state stayed 조립 and nothing touched a motor, the ASI or the camera. The claude.ai Figma connector needs authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used.","ttft_ms":1936,"type":"result","duration_ms":7670534,"uuid":"ffebb2b3-a40d-48eb-90cf-2652968e3451","ttft_stream_ms":1834,"time_to_request_ms":233,"first_content_frame_ms":1834,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
